# Copy to .env and paste a real key. .env is gitignored — keep it that way.
#
# Used ONLY to prefill the API key field during local development, so you are not
# retyping a key on every fresh browser profile. It is never auto-verified and never
# written to localStorage on your behalf.
#
# Get a key: https://portal.privatemode.ai
PRIVATEMODE_AI_API_KEY=

# ── How this reaches the browser ────────────────────────────────────────────
# A browser cannot read .env. Until the Vite build lands, generate the shim:
#
#   node make-env.mjs    # writes env.js from .env  (both are gitignored)
#
# Once Vite is in place this becomes VITE_HC_DEV_API_KEY, read through
# `import.meta.env.DEV && import.meta.env.VITE_HC_DEV_API_KEY`, so the branch is
# stripped from production builds entirely. See ARCHITECTURE.md §8.2 — a key baked
# into a bundle deployed to GitHub Pages would be public to everyone.
